  "scope": [
    "Root composition body/text and parser-tree capacities now use the render Node owner. A verified regular descriptor admits exact backing plus sentinel and UTF-16 decoding before allocation; remaining Node capacity controls root file admission while native files retain their fixed 32 MiB ceiling.",
    "Producer child scopes share the same counter and roll back only their own reservations on failure. Completed root/native products transfer to the render owner. Later failed binary verification preserves unrelated owners; closed child scopes reject new allocations.",
    "Exact plain-data JSON/UTF-8 sizing includes escaping, surrogate pairs/lone surrogates, finite numbers, omitted properties, array holes and pretty whitespace. Reject accessors/hooks/inherited array hooks/cycles before serialization. Root render and default composition scene manifests admit text and write encoding first; supplied text admits its write encoding.",
    "Descriptor errors/cancellation retire actual private backing and preserve the original cause, including null, through secondary close failure. Native growth/cancel cases now also verify backing detachment."
  ],
  "qualification": "Current held fast20/Node21 and actual PBR composition/normal/mixed plus all six native2 groups pass. Root read and scene serialization capacities are declared producer storage; semantic validation/diagnostic report allocations, other media/code-identity producers, final lifecycle/RSS and aggregate world/body/replay remain separate. Direct legacy non-composition exports keep their prior serialization route. Result callback/report producers retain earlier bounded protocol and still require the broader audit. No complete whole-Node/MS2 gate, final installed refresh, human acceptance or publication is claimed.",
